      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When a user submits a \"Right to be Forgotten\" request in Estonia under GDPR, a company must first verify the identity of the requestor. Next, the company needs to assess if there are legal grounds or overriding public interest reasons to refuse the erasure. If no such grounds exist, the organization must delete the personal data without undue delay and inform any third parties it shared the data with. Finally, you must log the entire request and erasure process for compliance auditing purposes.",
